    "### Chart 1 - Class Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "A class distribution chart shows how many images exist for each pen. The ideal situation is a perfectly balanced bar chart where every pen has the same number of images. In reality, imbalance is common.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why imbalance matters:** If pen 1 appears 5000 times and pen 8 appears only 200 times, the model can score 96% accuracy just by always predicting pen 1 - without ever learning anything about the other pens. Knowing this lets us decide whether to use class weights or oversampling to fix the problem."
